  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote `src/main.ts` and it passes `typecheck`. I couldn't run it in a browser or run `vite build` here, so the framing, shadow and crossfade are unverified at runtime.\n\n- **Model and framing:** `/assets/soldier.glb` is declared with `defineAuraAssets` and added with `model(..., { targetHeight: 1.8 })`. The engine fits it to the GLB's real bounds and puts its feet at y=0. It stands on a 16x16 `primitives.plane` ground. A fixed perspective camera at `[0, 1.35, 5.2]` looking at `[0, 0.88, 0]` should frame the whole character. I assumed the soldier faces +Z, toward the camera. If it doesn't, the first screenshot will show its back.\n- **Animation:** The model starts on `Idle`. `R` and `I` call `soldier.play(\"Run\" | \"Idle\", { crossFade: 0.4 })` on the runtime node. Crossfading depends on the engine's `A3D_QR_ANIMATION` flag, which I confirmed is default-on in this build. The key handler ignores key repeats and does nothing if that clip is already the target.\n- **Lighting:** There is one shadow-casting directional light with a 2048 shadow map. The fill lights (hemisphere and ambient) don't cast shadows. The ground receives shadows and doesn't cast them.\n- **Eval hooks:** `window.__EVAL__.clip()` returns the target clip name as soon as a fade starts. `window.__EVAL_READY__` becomes true once all assets report loaded and at least 3 frames have been drawn. A 15 s timeout sets it anyway so a failed load can't hang the harness.\n- **Canvas:** The app uses the existing `#app` canvas with `resize: false` and `pixelRatio: 1`, so it keeps its 640x360 size.\n\n",
  "finalTypecheckPass": true,
